  <h2 id="money-check">Money check before you pay for a course or degree</h2>

  <p>Our strongest suggestion: keep a course or degree fee near a tenth of the family education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs course-specific evidence. This does not apply to very cheap online courses. Free YouTube lessons and low-priced courses on sites like Udemy or Coursera need little budget care, and the same course through a university certificate can cost 30 to 100 times more.</p>
  <p>An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 3 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 30,000 for the main course and a fifth is Rs 60,000. Spend the rest on tools, practice and a reserve. This is general information, not financial advice, and you should avoid an education loan for a short course and get any loan terms in writing.</p>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Pick the lane by daily work first, then choose the employer type you will aim for and the one skill that moves you into a higher band. <strong>That is how a high-value skill portfolio, backed by proof of work, turns into higher pay and earlier financial freedom.</strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    For the wider choice, read our <a href="/blog/career-options/data-science-vs-software-engineering-career-india/">data science vs software engineering career comparison</a>. For each lane on its own, see <a href="/blog/career-options/is-data-science-a-good-career-in-india/">is data science a good career in India</a> and <a href="/blog/career-options/is-software-engineering-a-good-career-in-india/">is software engineering a good career in India</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you lean to data science, <a href="/blog/skills/skills-required-for-data-scientist-india/">the skills required for a data scientist in India</a> lays out what to build. To compare it with a model-building role, read <a href="/blog/ai-future/machine-learning-vs-data-science-career-path-india/">machine learning vs data science career path in India</a>. To see where you stand today, try the free <a href="/career-skills-compass/">Career &amp; Skills Compass</a>.
  </p>

